On Monday, rescuers from the Nepal National Mountain Guide Association said they had recovered two more bodies.

The association initially said 12 kitchen staff and two guides were missing before reporting that the guides had been found dead, leaving 12 people still missing by its count.

“Unfortunately, after extensive search efforts under extremely difficult conditions, four bodies were recovered, while 12 cook staff remain missing at Himlung Base Camp,” the association said.

