“The avalanche was exceptionally large, with approximately 14 feet of snow covering the Base Camp area. Searching every section manually was extremely difficult and dangerous due to the depth of snow, freezing temperatures, and unstable conditions,” the official added, releasing a video showing rescue workers digging through the snow.

Bibhuti Chand Thakur of Himalaya Holidays Trekking told the AFP news agency that eight members of his expedition team were missing.

